\title{twfeweights: Implicit Weights and Covariate Balance for Difference-in-Differences Estimators}
\description{
Computes the implicit weights that two-way fixed effects (TWFE) regressions and other difference-in-differences estimators place on group-time average treatment effects in staggered treatment adoption designs. Without covariates, the package recovers the weights that a TWFE regression places on each group-time average treatment effect (including pre-treatment periods), following de Chaisemartin and D'Haultfoeuille (2020) \doi{10.1257/aer.20181169} and Goodman-Bacon (2021) \doi{10.1016/j.jeconom.2021.03.014}, and compares them with the weights behind the overall average treatment effect parameters in Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021) \doi{10.1016/j.jeconom.2020.12.001}. With covariates, it writes TWFE regressions and augmented inverse probability weighting (AIPW), regression adjustment and inverse probability weighting estimators as reweighting estimators and reports how well the implied weights balance covariates across treated and comparison groups, as in Caetano and Callaway (2024) \doi{10.48550/arXiv.2406.15288}.
}
\details{
The package has three groups of functions.

\strong{Staggered adoption without covariates.} \code{\link[=twfe_weights]{twfe_weights()}} recovers the
weights that a TWFE regression places on each group-time average
treatment effect, \eqn{ATT(g,t)}, estimated by \code{\link[did:att_gt]{did::att_gt()}}.
\code{\link[=attO_weights]{attO_weights()}} and \code{\link[=att_simple_weights]{att_simple_weights()}} give the weights behind the
overall average treatment effects of Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021), for
comparison.

\strong{Covariates, two periods.} \code{\link[=two_period_reg_weights]{two_period_reg_weights()}} writes a TWFE
regression with covariates as a reweighting estimator;
\code{\link[=two_period_aipw_weights]{two_period_aipw_weights()}} does the same for AIPW, regression adjustment
and inverse probability weighting. Both report how well the implicit
weights balance covariates.

\strong{Covariates, staggered adoption.} \code{\link[=implicit_twfe_weights]{implicit_twfe_weights()}} and
\code{\link[=implicit_aipw_weights]{implicit_aipw_weights()}} extend these to many periods;
\code{\link[=twfe_cov_bal]{twfe_cov_bal()}} and \code{\link[=aipw_cov_bal]{aipw_cov_bal()}} compute covariate balance.

\code{\link[=ggtwfeweights]{ggtwfeweights()}} plots the results. \code{\link[=pooled_sd]{pooled_sd()}}, \code{\link[=log_ratio_sd]{log_ratio_sd()}},
\code{\link[=frac_treated_extreme]{frac_treated_extreme()}} and \code{\link[=effective_sample_size]{effective_sample_size()}} compute the
balance statistics and can be applied to any set of weights.

See \code{vignette("twfe-weights", package = "twfeweights")} and
\code{vignette("covariate-balance", package = "twfeweights")}.
}
